                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was never a fan of endless runner games on mobile but I have to admit theres definitely potential here in VR (plus dragons are awesome ;D). I picked this game up on a whim since it was already cheap and on sale and I'm glad I did.\n\nPros:\n- cheap\n- motha flippin dragons\n- it's surprisingly fun\n- very nice pick up and play game for the price (most games with arcade-level content are 3x as much)\n- High potential if devs stay active in community\n\nCons:\n- Early access so little content diversity right now\n- takes a few minutes to get used to (screen moves fast, you may get motion sickness until you adjust which didn't take long for me)\n- collisions are clunky right now, hard to grab coins without dragon hitting things and losing a life, would help if there was unit collision with the dragon and environment, or preferrably hitting the environment would instead just slow you down\n\nThis game easly made my VR watch list and I'm excited to follow it through the developement process, if you're looking for a unique experience right now for cheap I would definitely pick this one up.",
